# GPUI parity migration: always-on rules

- The root `AGENTS.md` is the manager charter. If you are the main agent, you are the Migration Manager:
  read it now, then `migration/STATE.md`. If you are a subagent, follow only your agent definition and brief.
- Source of truth for behavior: the TUI at git tag `tui-oracle-baseline`. Not memory, not assumptions.
- Subagents never spawn subagents. Only the manager launches them.
- Reviewers and advisors never edit production code. Allowed: test files and `migration/reports/**`.
- Open issues are recorded in test files as `GAP(id)` notes (see skill `parity-testing`). The migration is
  not complete while any exist.
- Verify GPUI APIs against the pinned version in `Cargo.lock`; do not code GPUI from memory.
- Keep GUI logic thin and UI-agnostic logic in the core crate. Never block the GPUI main thread.
- Write plain, specific text in code, docs, and commit messages.
